#
# Mid-director mouse-tracking escape hatch (coilysiren/agentic-os#320).
#
# A warded director TUI (Claude Code) can be poisoned by a child that enables
# xterm mouse-tracking (DECSET 1003) and exits without restoring it: the pane
# then floods with raw `^[[<35;X;YM` SGR motion reports. The pwsh-prompt reset
# (commit b562b4f) only fires between prompts, so it cannot heal while the
# director holds the terminal - today's only recovery is killing the director.
#
# `workspace:toggle_mouse_reporting` flips mouse reporting at the Warp emulator
# layer with zero cooperation from the director or any child, so pressing it
# stops the flood WITHOUT dropping the TUI. It is a toggle, not a one-way
# disable: one press clears a stuck-on flood, a second press re-enables legit
# TUI mouse use. That is fine for an escape hatch.
"workspace:toggle_mouse_reporting": "ctrl-shift-m"
